From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "vlad.maglasu" <vlad.maglasu@vampirebyte.ro>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 10:37:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(libslac): port EVerest main's EVSE SLAC fixes onto
 fsm::v2

Brings the fsm::v2 EVSE machine in line with the fixes EVerest main made to the
Boost.MSM one since fsm::v2 was branched.

EVerest/EVerest#3166 (no log of the session NMK): Reset no longer logs the
session NMK it programs.

EVerest/EVerest#3328 (session NMK with full entropy): Reset generates the NMK
through Context::generate_nmk(), which warns once when std::random_device is
unavailable and the key is seeded from the clock.

EVerest/EVerest#3334 (CM_VALIDATE bound to the EV's own session): a
CM_VALIDATE.REQ is answered only for an EV with a session waiting for its
CM_SLAC_MATCH.REQ ([V2G3-A09-75], [V2G3-A09-85]). The TT_match_sequence window
after a completed validation ([V2G3-A09-89], [V2G3-A09-90]) belongs to that
session instead of the Matching-wide context, and is armed only after at least
one BCB toggle was seen.

EVerest/EVerest#3133 (MATCHING published on the first CM_SLAC_PARM.REQ): the
armed Matching state publishes UNMATCHED; the first CM_SLAC_PARM.REQ publishes
MATCHING ([V2G3-M06-08]). A failed attempt with reset_instead_of_fail keeps
MATCHING while the EV retries.

Signed-off-by: vlad.maglasu <vlad.maglasu@vampirebyte.ro>

